flowchart LR

ROW2["`🛡️ THE BEHAVIOUR — what the user sees at the edge of capacity`"]
  R4["`NO ORPHANS
the planner runs BEFORE any write
invalid roadmap → 502/503,
nothing to clean up
the sequence IS the rollback`"]
ROW2 -.- R4
  R5["`PARTIAL IS A DELIBERATE STATE
item 31 failing must not
destroy the other 39
the teacher keeps what worked`"]
  R4 -.- R5 -.- R6
  R6["`GRACEFUL DEGRADATION, MEASURED
100 → 300 users: latency grows
~linearly, failures stay at ZERO,
the container stays healthy
Restarts=0 · OOMKilled=false
in EVERY run, including the one
with 89% failures
it degrades and refuses.
it does not fall over.`"]

ROW1["`🛡️ THE MECHANISMS — a senior system is one that fails well`"]
  R1["`CIRCUIT BREAKER, STATE IN REDIS
in-memory → every replica rediscovers
the outage by hammering a dead
endpoint, N times, once per process
in Redis → the whole FLEET shares
ONE view of 'this provider is down'
worthless at 1 replica, large at 50:
made for the system
that does not exist yet`"]
ROW1 -.- R1
  R2["`IDEMPOTENCY + task_acks_late
they only work TOGETHER
acks_late alone → duplicated work
idempotency alone → documents lost
on every worker crash
redelivery of PROCESSING/INDEXED
is a no-op, so a worker dying
mid-task loses nothing`"]
  R3["`RETRY 15s → 30s → 60s
→ FAILED + reason,
visible at /documents/{id}/status
infinite retry is a clogged queue;
a visible failure is a support team
that can actually answer the teacher`"]
  R1 -.- R2 -.- R3 -.- R7
  R7["`NO POOLED DB CONNECTION HELD
DURING AN LLM CALL
a chain can run for minutes
holding one would starve every
other route — and the symptom would
appear on endpoints with nothing
to do with AI. You would spend
the night in the wrong place.`"]

FLAW["`MY OWN SYSTEM'S FLAW — I present it before you find it

an exhausted DB pool returns 500 today. It should be 503 + Retry-After, because it is BACKPRESSURE, not an error.
Consequence 1: the client and the load balancer never learn to back off.
Consequence 2, and this is the worse one: on the dashboard those 500s are indistinguishable from a real bug —
I polluted my own error signal with load.

Written down in perf/RESULTS.md. One status code, one exception handler.`"]

